Subject: [LOCAL CANDIDATE] Timestamp virtual capture using frame presentation

The monitor source uses Clutter's target presentation timestamp. The virtual
source instead samples the clock after rendering, so render-duration jitter
feeds the minimum-interval limiter. Use the same timestamp selection as the
monitor source, with the existing monotonic-clock fallback. Not deployed until
private and live validation pass. This does not disable the negotiated cap.

--- a/src/backends/meta-screen-cast-virtual-stream-src.c
+++ b/src/backends/meta-screen-cast-virtual-stream-src.c
@@ -207,12 +207,18 @@
   MetaScreenCastStreamSrc *src = META_SCREEN_CAST_STREAM_SRC (user_data);
   MetaScreenCastPaintPhase paint_phase;
   MetaScreenCastRecordFlag flags;
+  int64_t presentation_time_us;
+
+  if (!clutter_frame_get_target_presentation_time (frame, &presentation_time_us))
+    presentation_time_us = g_get_monotonic_time ();
 
   flags = META_SCREEN_CAST_RECORD_FLAG_NONE;
   paint_phase = META_SCREEN_CAST_PAINT_PHASE_PRE_SWAP_BUFFER;
-  meta_screen_cast_stream_src_maybe_record_frame (src, flags,
-                                                  paint_phase,
-                                                  redraw_clip);
+  meta_screen_cast_stream_src_maybe_record_frame_with_timestamp (src,
+                                                                 flags,
+                                                                 paint_phase,
+                                                                 redraw_clip,
+                                                                 presentation_time_us);
 }
 
 static void
